# QA changelog after push

Whenever you successfully push a release or deploy commit to GitHub (especially via the git-push skill), end the reply with a **changelog-style summary for the QA team** pasted in the chat.

## Required format

```markdown
## [VERSION] — YYYY-MM-DD

### Added
- …

### Changed
- …

### Fixed
- …
```

Omit empty sections. Prefer concise, testable, user-facing bullets. Drop internal-only paths/helper names unless QA needs them.

Lead with branch, commit hash, and version, then the full block. Do not only link to `CHANGELOG.md`.
